  "expected_answer": "Brief saved, state written, brand set; the line stops at keys: EXA_API_KEY (and MODEL_API_KEY / RESEND_API_KEY unless reused from an app that already runs) must be typed by the operator at a hidden prompt: python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret EXA_API_KEY.",
  "final_text": "I've minted Harbor Desk. It stopped at the first step that needs you: its service keys.\n\n**Done:**\n- **Brief** saved to `briefs/harbor_desk.md`, exactly as you wrote it.\n- **App records** created and checked. It will go on Vercel under the project name `harbor-desk`, with the workspace \"Harbor Pilots\". The owner is owner@harbor.example, and ana@ and raj@ are members. Web search is on and the browser is off, as the brief asked.\n- **Branding** set to the name Harbor Desk and the colour #0B6E4F.\n- No custom code bundle, extra workspace, published package or custom web address is needed, so those steps are skipped.\n\n**Where it stopped:** six service keys aren't set yet: `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, `PLATFORM_NOTIFY_FROM`, `EXA_API_KEY` and `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`.\n\nThe quickest way is to copy them from an app of yours that already runs. The only finished app on this machine is **beta_app**, but it belongs to a different workspace (Beta Ops, owner@beta.example). I didn't want to put one workspace's keys into another without your say-so, so I haven't copied them. Please pick one:\n\n1. **The keys belong to you and can be shared.** Say \"reuse beta_app's keys\". I'll copy them over in memory; the values never appear in this chat or in any file.\n2. **Harbor Desk needs its own keys.** Then you enter them one at a time in a separate terminal on this machine (not this chat). The first one is:\n   ```\n   python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID\n   ```\n   It tells you where to find the value and asks for it at a hidden prompt, so nothing shows on screen. Tell me when it's done and I'll give you the next one.\n\n**After the keys:**\n- **Putting it live on Vercel** takes about 10 minutes. I'll ask for a plain yes before I start it.\n- **The tests** take about 30 minutes, and the ones that need a signed-in person need a one-time code from someone who can sign in.",
